      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix",
      "problem": "Find the value of $|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =-2|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(4-0)-1(1-0)-1(-3-20) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-23) \\\\  & =-8-1-23 \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$",
